# Force LF line endings for AgentEval workspace artefacts so SHA-256 content
# hashes are deterministic across Windows/macOS/Linux runners.
# .NET 9+ also pins JsonSerializerOptions.NewLine = "\n" on the writer side;
# this attribute is belt-and-braces for files that are committed (e.g.
# compliance/, baseline.json, history.jsonl, subject.json).
.agenteval/**/*.json   text eol=lf
.agenteval/**/*.jsonl  text eol=lf
src/AgentEval.DataLoaders/Output/Schema/v1/*.json text eol=lf
# The time-grounded corpus is embedded and content-hashed into run provenance, so its
# bytes must not depend on which platform checked it out. LongMemEvalTimeGroundedCorpus
# also normalizes newlines before hashing; this keeps the two from ever disagreeing.
src/AgentEval.Memory/Data/longmemeval/timegrounded/*.json text eol=lf
# Same reason for the TypedMemEval family corpora: each one is content-hashed into run
# provenance, and its metadata sidecar records the hash it describes, so a CRLF checkout must
# not make the two disagree.
src/AgentEval.Memory/Data/typedmemeval/**/*.json text eol=lf
